@startuml Hexagonal_Adjudication
title Hexagonal Architecture — representative context: Adjudication (all greenfield contexts follow this shape)

hexagon "DOMAIN (pure PHP — zero Illuminate)\n\nDetermination aggregate\nValue Objects · DeterminationIssued\nLegitimacyDecision (domain service)\nDeterminationRepository (port)\nexceptions" as DOM #lightgreen

rectangle "APPLICATION (orchestration only, ADR-T17)\nAdjudicationService (port) ← TransactionalAdjudicationService ← CoordinatesAdjudication\nports: TransactionManager · IdentityGenerator · EventOutbox" as APP #lightblue

rectangle "INFRASTRUCTURE (Laravel allowed)\nEloquentDeterminationRepository + Model + Mapper\nLaravelTransactionManager · UuidIdentityGenerator\nOutboxEventAdapter · DeterminationIssuedHydrator\nAdjudicationServiceProvider" as INF #lightyellow

rectangle "DRIVING adapters\nHTTP controller / console / future handlers" as DRV
rectangle "DRIVEN systems\nPostgreSQL · outbox_events\nEventHydratorRegistry (shared)" as EXT

DRV --> APP : commands (IssueDeterminationCommand — DTO, no arrays)
APP --> DOM : invokes aggregate + domain service
APP --> DOM : depends on repository PORT (interface in Domain)
INF --> DOM : implements ports (dependency points INWARD)
INF --> EXT : SQL / rows
APP ..> INF : never directly — only via container-bound ports

note bottom
  Rule of the shape: Domain depends on NOTHING. Application depends on Domain.
  Infrastructure depends on both and is the only place Laravel exists.
  Enforced by: GreenfieldCoreArchitectureTest · phpstan-greenfield.neon ·
  Deptrac (pending F-1) · domain-purity architecture tests.
end note
@enduml
